      en: "Péhunco is a town in northwestern Benin, in the Atakora Department, near the Pendjari River, forming the border with Burkina Faso. It is the capital of Péhunco Commune. The population is mainly Gourmantché and Bariba. The economy is based on agriculture (cotton, maize, yam) and fishing. Péhunco is an important border trading center. The town has a health center, primary schools, and a market. The region features savanna and floodplains. Annual rainfall is about 1,000 mm. The dry season lasts from November to April.",
